    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by an elite spot start for **Corbin Carroll**, who leads our lineup with a 77.63 score. The combination of a favorable matchup against McGreevy (4.43 xERA) and an elevated batting order position makes him our primary engine for R and SB production today. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (66.63) presents a strong start; he benefits from a pronounced dynamic platoon advantage against Melton, allowing his base projection to climb significantly as he occupies the heart of the order. **Gabriel Moreno** rounds out our top-tier plays at 60.15, as his recent hot streak and the +10% SP skill bump from the McGreevy matchup solidify him as a high-floor selection behind the dish.\n\nThe optimizer faced its tightest margin between the start of **Austin Riley** (53.73) and our bench depth. While **Riley** faces a tougher matchup against Hart (3.98 xERA), his consistent underlying profile held off any potential swap with **Isaac Paredes** or **Max Muncy**. **Zach McKinstry** (53.82) survives the cut despite an #8 spot in the order, largely because the matchup against Dobnak (5.65 xERA) provides an exceptionally high ceiling for counting stats that offsets his lackluster lineup placement. Meanwhile, **Travis Bazzana** (47.51) remains our most volatile start; while his platoon advantage against Bradley provides a decent floor, he is on a short leash to preserve our game caps if he fails to capitalize early.\n\nWe are navigating several roster dead zones today, as **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, and **Mickey Moniak** are all sidelined by team off-days, leaving our depth options like **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** to rest while we monitor the impact of **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential spot-start value in upcoming series. No major weather concerns have been flagged for our active starters, but we are keeping a close watch on the official batting order confirmations for **McKinstry** and **Bazzana** to ensure their projected slots hold, as any downward movement in the order would immediately drop them into sub-40, bench-worthy territory.",
